{"data": [{"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-04T21:34:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118094439822623024"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/brivael/status…", "end": 294, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/brivael/status/2117917230394376467", "start": 271, "url": "https://t.co/Cb1ZbezdUO"}]}, "id": "2118094439822623024", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 963, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117917230394376467", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "It's not easy or politically costless, and am open to the possibility that it's harder than in the past, but the claim that \"the government can't fix its own deficit\" is flatly belied by the historical record which includes plenty of successful deficit reduction efforts https://t.co/Cb1ZbezdUO", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2118094439822623024"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-04T21:12:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118088953924325614"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MFK75XdbYJ", "end": 279, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118088953924325614/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118088831953973249", "start": 256, "url": "https://t.co/MFK75XdbYJ"}]}, "id": "2118088953924325614", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 3794, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "For those interested in the simple effective tariff rate (tariffs collected divided by imports, so this misses the impact of a prohibitive tariff), see the chart below\n\nThe effective tariff on China is now down to around 20%, + 10% in the second term\n\n1/2 https://t.co/MFK75XdbYJ", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118088953924325614"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-04T20:57:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118085220230643764"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/lPLL0t2wnt", "end": 230, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2118085220230643764/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118085206129487872", "start": 207, "url": "https://t.co/lPLL0t2wnt"}]}, "id": "2118085220230643764", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1271, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Indeed job postings update:\n\n1/ Software postings still zooming... at recent growth rates, less than a year away from returning to their pre-pandemic level.  (Obviously the post-pandemic peak is eons away.) https://t.co/lPLL0t2wnt", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2118085220230643764"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-04T20:50:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118083443519361059"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/rOqS2SxW9d", "end": 272, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118083443519361059/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118083436191657984", "start": 249, "url": "https://t.co/rOqS2SxW9d"}]}, "id": "2118083443519361059", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 5622, "like_count": 11, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "The amount of volatility in the US trade deficit (and specifically the non-petrol deficit) in the last 7 years has been kind of crazy -- COVID, the surge in goods imports during the lockdown, tariff front running, and now the crazy AI spend ...\n\n1/ https://t.co/rOqS2SxW9d", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2118083443519361059"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "702235316812275712", "name": "Guy Berger", "username": "EconBerger"}, {"id": "733647469305864195", "name": "Brad Setser", "username": "Brad_Setser"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2118094439822623024", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyxaq3vqtykefnjnto7ogtvxx19", "oldest_id": "2118083443519361059", "result_count": 4}}
